ion \"Staff Engineer Input Disposition\" listing the overrides: (1) action file count corrected to 15 across 4 tiers (8 component, 3 service, 1 DSC, 3 module) — decomposition uses corrected counts; (2) module controller tier with 8 module handlers added to scope (HLR-6 covered in manager epic); (3) \"~16 component action files\" open question resolved (8/8 confirmed) — not treated as unknown; (4) camelCase convention, cloudmanager shared reconciler, cluster-scoped AC confirmed as-is.\n\nHealth warnings:\n1. Epic size overage (E001) with re-split trigger.\n2. DSCI key migration replaces queryable field names — existing Loki/CloudWatch queries on Request.Name/DSCInitialization will break; mitigation single-release transition + release notes (recorded as AC/notes on E001; also E002 not affected). This is more a risk note than a warning; fine to include.\n3. Open question dispositions (why no Investigation epics) — I'll put under a section \"Open Question Disposition\".\n4. External adoption (COO) is voluntary — no epic can gate it.\n\nAlso the \"publish early\" tension with Rule 11: docs epic runs last per Rule 11, while a risk mitigation suggests publishing the convention early for external adoption. Hmm — should I flag this? I could note it as a health warning: \"Risk mitigation suggests publishing the convention early to COO; per Rule 11 the docs-authoring epic is sequenced after implementation epics because the guideline includes before/after examples drawn from the implemented conversion. If early publication becomes critical, the publication note to COO teams can be sent independently by the team without restructuring this DAG.\" That's a reasonable note. Include briefly.\n\nNow write everything. Let me create the files.\n\nEpic count and IDs: E001 manager, E002 cloudmanager, E003 docs.\n\nMermaid DAG:\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    E001[\"E001 manager binary log standardization\"] --> E003[\"E003 convention documentation and publication\"]\n    E002[\"E002 cloudmanager log standardization\"] --> E003\n```\n\nKeep simple: E001 --> E003; E002 --> E003.\n\nDAG Justification table:\n| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n| E001 → E003 | Rule 11 | docs-authoring blocked by all Implementation epics; guideline documents the implemented convention incl. before/after examples |\n| E002 → E003 | Rule 11 | same |\n| (no edge) E001 ∥ E002 | Rule 15 | same repo, different binaries/areas; parallel; merge-conflict coordination risk only |\n\nNow write files. I'll use Write tool for bodies.","signature":"990017922cc249e7bc10f13fbc1d65f0"}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":42710,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b715a6c9be533eb8","agent_id":"a7fb5fe8d67ee6696","session_id":"97c222b8-155b-40d2-9c11-f4c45b15208c","uuid":"5687bfe8-54ee-4056-9816-112d9ae107dc","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:27:16.520Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8010"}
