{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-1d3466a2-ccc6-4f44-bcfd-2d31fc548b03","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-938a41f1ec47c001","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-yl27p7nu/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8010-E001.md","content":"# Standardize manager binary reconciliation error logs with structured resource context\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic converts message-embedded resource identity to structured key-value pairs and\nadds the `resourceKind` field across all reconciliation error logging in the rhods-operator\nmanager binary. It delivers the three fixes diagnosed in the strategy for the manager\nbinary: (1) reconciliation error logs that embed resource name or namespace in the message\nstring are converted to structured `name`/`namespace` key-value pairs, (2) the\nDSCInitialization controller is migrated from the non-standard key names `Request.Name` and\n`DSCInitialization` to the standard camelCase convention (`name`, `namespace`,\n`resourceKind`), and (3) `resourceKind` is added to all reconciliation error logs,\nincluding controllers whose reconciler name does not imply the kind (service controllers,\nmodule controller and its handlers, action files). A CI lint rule locks the convention in\nfor future development, and a log-consumer regression validation protects existing\ningestion pipelines and text-based alert rules.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Audit all `log.Error()` call sites in reconciliation error paths across the manager\n  binary's five controller tiers:\n  - the DataScienceCluster (DSC) controller,\n  - 8 component controllers (DataSciencePipelines, Kueue, ModelRegistry, Ray,\n    SparkOperator, Trainer, TrainingOperator, TrustyAI),\n  - the module controller with its 8 module handlers (Dashboard, AIGateway, KServe, OGX,\n    Workbenches, MLflowOperator, FeastOperator, MCPLifecycleOperator),\n  - the DSCInitialization (DSCI) controller,\n  - 5 service controllers (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup).\n- Audit and convert the 15 action files across four tiers: 8 component action files\n  (`components/<name>/<name>_controller_actions.go`), 3 service action files\n  (`services/{auth,gateway,monitoring}/*_controller_actions.go`), 1 DSC action file\n  (`datasciencecluster/datasciencecluster_controller_actions.go`), and 3 module action\n  files (`modules/modules_controller_actions*.go`).\n- For every call site embedding resource name or namespace in the message string, extract\n  the identity fields and convert to structured key-value pairs\n  (`\"name\", <obj>.Name, \"namespace\", <obj>.Namespace`), removing the redundant identity\n  from the message text.\n- Add `resourceKind` as a structured field to all reconciliation error logs: required for\n  service controllers, the module controller and its handlers, and all action files (kind\n  not implied by controller name), and for the DSC and 8 component controllers (bundled P1\n  queryability enhancement over the same call sites).\n- Migrate DSCI structured field names from `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` to\n  `name`/`namespace` (per Staff Engineer input, at `dscinitialization_controller.go:154,169,182`).\n- Handle cluster-scoped resources (e.g., DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization): emit\n  `name` and `resourceKind`, with `namespace` omitted or set to empty string — no spurious\n  namespace value.\n- Add a CI lint/static-analysis rule that flags any `log.Error` call embedding\n  name/namespace in message text or missing the required structured fields.\n- Add unit tests asserting field presence and correctness via test logger output.\n- Log-consumer regression validation: before/after log output comparison for a sample\n  reconciliation error; deploy a test build to a dev cluster with the production log\n  consumer stack configured and verify ingestion; coordinate with SRE/Support to identify\n  text-based alert rules that rely on the changed message-string patterns and track their\n  updates.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Static analysis (grep/lint) over the manager binary finds zero `log.Error`\n  reconciliation-error call sites that embed resource name or namespace in the message\n  string; every such site emits `name` and `namespace` as structured key-value pairs.\n- Unit tests assert DSCI error logs contain the standard field names (`name`,\n  `namespace`, `resourceKind`), and a codebase grep confirms no references to the old\n  field names `Request.Name` and `DSCInitialization` remain.\n- Unit tests parsing test logger output assert `resourceKind` is present with the correct\n  value for error logs from all 5 service controllers (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring,\n  CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup), the module controller and its 8 module handlers, and all\n  15 action files across the 4 tiers.\n- Unit tests assert DSC and 8 component controller reconciliation error logs include\n  `resourceKind`.\n- A unit test confirms cluster-scoped resources (e.g., DataScienceCluster,\n  DSCInitialization) do not emit a spurious namespace value.\n- The CI lint rule is merged and demonstrably fails on a deliberately non-conforming\n  `log.Error` call (test fixture) while passing on the converted codebase.\n- A before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error is documented,\n  showing structured fields present and the message-text change, and confirming the log\n  consumer (e.g., Loki) ingests both formats without configuration changes.\n- Text-based alert rules relying on the changed message-string patterns are identified\n  with SRE/Support, and each identified rule is recorded and tracked for update.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 [P0]: reconciliation error logs embedding name/namespace in message strings\n  converted to structured key-value pairs (manager binary portion).\n- HLR-2 [P0]: DSCI controller migrated from `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` to\n  camelCase `name`/`namespace`.\n- HLR-3 [P0]: service controller error logs include `resourceKind`.\n- HLR-4 [P0]: all 15 action file error logs include `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`\n  across the 4 tiers (8 component + 3 service + 1 DSC + 3 module).\n- HLR-6 [P0]: module controller error logs include `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`\n  (8 module handlers).\n- HLR-7 [P1] (bundled): DSC and component controller error logs include `resourceKind` —\n  bundled because it edits the same `log.Error` call sites, shares the same audit pass and\n  CI lint rule as the P0 conversion work; splitting would double-touch every call site.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Inconsistent adoption across the five controller tiers and 15 action files: mitigated by\n  the grep/static-analysis audit with a coverage checklist and the CI lint rule gating new\n  code.\n- DSCI key-name migration replaces existing queryable field names: existing Loki/CloudWatch\n  queries filtering on `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` will break. The transition is\n  completed in a single release, and the migration is documented in release notes with\n  before/after query examples (expanded in the convention documentation epic).\n- Log consumer regression: addressed by the dev-cluster validation and SRE/Support alert\n  rule identification above.\n- The actual percentage of log calls embedding resource identity (SME estimate 75%) is\n  confirmed by this epic's audit; the conversion covers all embedding sites regardless of\n  the percentage.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":49674,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b715a6c9be533eb8","agent_id":"a7fb5fe8d67ee6696","session_id":"97c222b8-155b-40d2-9c11-f4c45b15208c","uuid":"a3c19145-e8c8-434e-8d09-444eb5fd6fe7","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:28:09.450Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8010"}
