{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-7ab4ca68-2d2a-4e01-b92c-c50cf2fe4fe4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7ec1ccee71eaca5","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-yl27p7nu/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8010-E003.md","content":"# Document and publish the structured reconciliation log field convention\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic authors and publishes the structured reconciliation log field convention as a\ncontribution guideline for new controller development, and publishes it for external\noperator adoption. It documents the required fields (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`),\nthe camelCase naming rationale, the three-problem diagnosis that motivated the standard\n(message-embedded identity, non-standard DSCI keys, missing `resourceKind`), before/after\ncode examples drawn from the implemented conversion, and the DSCI key-name migration guide.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Author a contribution guideline specifying:\n  - the required structured fields (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`) for reconciliation\n    error logs, including treatment of cluster-scoped resources (namespace omitted or\n    empty),\n  - the camelCase naming rationale (alignment with controller-runtime's structured log key\n    conventions),\n  - the three-problem diagnosis (message-embedded identity, non-standard DSCI keys\n    `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization`, missing `resourceKind`),\n  - before/after code examples for converting message-embedded resource identity to\n    structured key-value pairs, taken from the implemented conversion in the manager and\n    cloudmanager binaries,\n  - the DSCI key-name migration guide with before/after query examples for operators using\n    Loki/CloudWatch queries that filtered on the old field names.\n- Resolve, with PM / Observability team input, whether the convention should include\n  fields beyond name/namespace/kind (e.g., reconciliation attempt count, error category)\n  and document the decision — either included with rationale or explicitly deferred\n  (weighing utility against log volume).\n- Publish the convention as a specification for voluntary adoption by external operator\n  teams — the Cluster Observability Operator team's Loki Operator and Tempo Operator — per\n  platform policy (overlay 0008: RHOAI does not install, manage, or control external\n  operator dependencies).\n- File tracking issues in the COO projects for the convention's adoption, accepting that\n  external adoption is best-effort.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The contribution guideline exists, specifying the required fields (`name`, `namespace`,\n  `resourceKind`), the camelCase naming rationale, and the three-problem diagnosis.\n- The guideline includes before/after code examples for converting message-embedded\n  resource identity to structured key-value pairs, and a DSCI key migration guide with\n  before/after query examples.\n- The decision on additional convention fields (e.g., reconciliation attempt count, error\n  category) is recorded with PM/Observability input: either included in the guideline with\n  rationale or explicitly deferred with rationale.\n- The convention is published for external operator adoption and tracking issues are filed\n  in the COO (Loki Operator, Tempo Operator) projects.\n- The guideline is technically reviewed against the implemented logging changes in the\n  manager and cloudmanager binaries (examples match the shipped code, field names match the\n  implementation).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-8 [P1]: document the convention as a contribution guideline for new controller\n  development and publish for external operator adoption.\n- Strategy acceptance criterion: the structured log field convention is documented in a\n  contribution guideline specifying required fields, camelCase naming rationale, and the\n  three-problem diagnosis.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- External operator adoption delay: the COO team may not prioritize adoption of the\n  convention. Mitigation: publish the convention and file tracking issues; adoption is\n  best-effort per platform policy (overlay 0008) and outside this strategy's control.\n- This epic must run after the code conversion in both binaries so its before/after\n  examples and migration guide reflect the implemented convention.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":52312,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b715a6c9be533eb8","agent_id":"a7fb5fe8d67ee6696","session_id":"97c222b8-155b-40d2-9c11-f4c45b15208c","uuid":"b8a02397-3105-422c-8154-c681a0556e6c","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:28:39.675Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8010"}
