{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a098fa09644e45b4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E001\n3\ttitle: Standardize manager binary reconciliation error logs with structured resource\n4\t  context\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n6\tcomponent: OpenShift AI Productization\n7\tteam: ODH Operator team\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies: []\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 1\n17\t  external_dependency: 0\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 6\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Standardize manager binary reconciliation error logs with structured resource context\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThis epic converts message-embedded resource identity to structured key-value pairs and\n35\tadds the `resourceKind` field across all reconciliation error logging in the rhods-operator\n36\tmanager binary. It delivers the three fixes diagnosed in the strategy for the manager\n37\tbinary: (1) reconciliation error logs that embed resource name or namespace in the message\n38\tstring are converted to structured `name`/`namespace` key-value pairs, (2) the\n39\tDSCInitialization controller is migrated from the non-standard key names `Request.Name` and\n40\t`DSCInitialization` to the standard camelCase convention (`name`, `namespace`,\n41\t`resourceKind`), and (3) `resourceKind` is added to all reconciliation error logs,\n42\tincluding controllers whose reconciler name does not imply the kind (service controllers,\n43\tmodule controller and its handlers, action files). A CI lint rule locks the convention in\n44\tfor future development, and a log-consumer regression validation protects existing\n45\tingestion pipelines and text-based alert rules.\n46\t\n47\t## Scope\n48\t\n49\t- Audit all `log.Error()` call sites in reconciliation error paths across the manager\n50\t  binary's five controller tiers:\n51\t  - the DataScienceCluster (DSC) controller,\n52\t  - 8 component controllers (DataSciencePipelines, Kueue, ModelRegistry, Ray,\n53\t    SparkOperator, Trainer, TrainingOperator, TrustyAI),\n54\t  - the module controller with its 8 module handlers (Dashboard, AIGateway, KServe, OGX,\n55\t    Workbenches, MLflowOperator, FeastOperator, MCPLifecycleOperator),\n56\t  - the DSCInitialization (DSCI) controller,\n57\t  - 5 service controllers (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup).\n58\t- Audit and convert the 15 action files across four tiers: 8 component action files\n59\t  (`components/<name>/<name>_controller_actions.go`), 3 service action files\n60\t  (`services/{auth,gateway,monitoring}/*_controller_actions.go`), 1 DSC action file\n61\t  (`datasciencecluster/datasciencecluster_controller_actions.go`), and 3 module action\n62\t  files (`modules/modules_controller_actions*.go`).\n63\t- For every call site embedding resource name or namespace in the message string, extract\n64\t  the identity fields and convert to structured key-value pairs\n65\t  (`\"name\", <obj>.Name, \"namespace\", <obj>.Namespace`), removing the redundant identity\n66\t  from the message text.\n67\t- Add `resourceKind` as a structured field to all reconciliation error logs: required for\n68\t  service controllers, the module controller and its handlers, and all action files (kind\n69\t  not implied by controller name), and for the DSC and 8 component controllers (bundled P1\n70\t  queryability enhancement over the same call sites).\n71\t- Migrate DSCI structured field names from `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` to\n72\t  `name`/`namespace` (per Staff Engineer input, at `dscinitialization_controller.go:154,169,182`).\n73\t- Handle cluster-scoped resources (e.g., DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization): emit\n74\t  `name` and `resourceKind`, with `namespace` omitted or set to empty string — no spurious\n75\t  namespace value.\n76\t- Add a CI lint/static-analysis rule that flags any `log.Error` call embedding\n77\t  name/namespace in message text or missing the required structured fields.\n78\t- Add unit tests asserting field presence and correctness via test logger output.\n79\t- Log-consumer regression validation: before/after log output comparison for a sample\n80\t  reconciliation error; deploy a test build to a dev cluster with the production log\n81\t  consumer stack configured and verify ingestion; coordinate with SRE/Support to identify\n82\t  text-based alert rules that rely on the changed message-string patterns and track their\n83\t  updates.\n84\t\n85\t## Acceptance Criteria\n86\t\n87\t- Static analysis (grep/lint) over the manager binary finds zero `log.Error`\n88\t  reconciliation-error call sites that embed resource name or namespace in the message\n89\t  string; every such site emits `name` and `namespace` as structured key-value pairs.\n90\t- Unit tests assert DSCI error logs contain the standard field names (`name`,\n91\t  `namespace`, `resourceKind`), and a codebase grep confirms no references to the old\n92\t  field names `Request.Name` and `DSCInitialization` remain.\n93\t- Unit tests parsing test logger output assert `resourceKind` is present with the correct\n94\t  value for error logs from all 5 service controllers (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring,\n95\t  CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup), the module controller and its 8 module handlers, and all\n96\t  15 action files across the 4 tiers.\n97\t- Unit tests assert DSC and 8 component controller reconciliation error logs include\n98\t  `resourceKind`.\n99\t- A unit test confirms cluster-scoped resources (e.g., DataScienceCluster,\n100\t  DSCInitialization) do not emit a spurious namespace value.\n101\t- The CI lint rule is merged and demonstrably fails on a deliberately non-conforming\n102\t  `log.Error` call (test fixture) while passing on the converted codebase.\n103\t- A before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error is documented,\n104\t  showing structured fields present and the message-text change, and confirming the log\n105\t  consumer (e.g., Loki) ingests both formats without configuration changes.\n106\t- Text-based alert rules relying on the changed message-string patterns are identified\n107\t  with SRE/Support, and each identified rule is recorded and tracked for update.\n108\t\n109\t## HLR Traceability\n110\t\n111\t- HLR-1 [P0]: reconciliation error logs embedding name/namespace in message strings\n112\t  converted to structured key-value pairs (manager binary portion).\n113\t- HLR-2 [P0]: DSCI controller migrated from `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` to\n114\t  camelCase `name`/`namespace`.\n115\t- HLR-3 [P0]: service controller error logs include `resourceKind`.\n116\t- HLR-4 [P0]: all 15 action file error logs include `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`\n117\t  across the 4 tiers (8 component + 3 service + 1 DSC + 3 module).\n118\t- HLR-6 [P0]: module controller error logs include `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`\n119\t  (8 module handlers).\n120\t- HLR-7 [P1] (bundled): DSC and component controller error logs include `resourceKind` —\n121\t  bundled because it edits the same `log.Error` call sites, shares the same audit pass and\n122\t  CI lint rule as the P0 conversion work; splitting would double-touch every call site.\n123\t\n124\t## Risks / Notes\n125\t\n126\t- Inconsistent adoption across the five controller tiers and 15 action files: mitigated by\n127\t  the grep/static-analysis audit with a coverage checklist and the CI lint rule gating new\n128\t  code.\n129\t- DSCI key-name migration replaces existing queryable field names: existing Loki/CloudWatch\n130\t  queries filtering on `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` will break. The transition is\n131\t  completed in a single release, and the migration is documented in release notes with\n132\t  before/after query examples (expanded in the convention documentation epic).\n133\t- Log consumer regression: addressed by the dev-cluster validation and SRE/Support alert\n134\t  rule identification above.\n135\t- The actual percentage of log calls embedding resource identity (SME estimate 75%) is\n136\t  confirmed by this epic's audit; the conversion covers all embedding sites regardless of\n137\t  the percentage.\n138\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d89b3ac798303c4","agent_id":"a677d7f0bb66f1eae","session_id":"97c222b8-155b-40d2-9c11-f4c45b15208c","uuid":"9ce9abc5-d9fe-477c-9296-d378dbe44efc","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:31:16.636Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a098fa09644e45b4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
