{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9053212bb5a352eb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E003\n3\ttitle: Document and publish the structured reconciliation log field convention\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n5\tcomponent: OpenShift AI Productization\n6\tteam: ODH Operator team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8010-E001\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8010-E002\n13\tai_signals:\n14\t  change_specificity: 1\n15\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n16\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n17\t  existing_foundation: 1\n18\t  open_questions: -1\n19\t  external_dependency: 0\n20\t  human_process_gates: -1\n21\t  repo_access: 1\n22\t  architecture_claims: 1\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: Medium\n25\tai_implementability_score: 2\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# Document and publish the structured reconciliation log field convention\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tThis epic authors and publishes the structured reconciliation log field convention as a\n36\tcontribution guideline for new controller development, and publishes it for external\n37\toperator adoption. It documents the required fields (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`),\n38\tthe camelCase naming rationale, the three-problem diagnosis that motivated the standard\n39\t(message-embedded identity, non-standard DSCI keys, missing `resourceKind`), before/after\n40\tcode examples drawn from the implemented conversion, and the DSCI key-name migration guide.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Author a contribution guideline specifying:\n45\t  - the required structured fields (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`) for reconciliation\n46\t    error logs, including treatment of cluster-scoped resources (namespace omitted or\n47\t    empty),\n48\t  - the camelCase naming rationale (alignment with controller-runtime's structured log key\n49\t    conventions),\n50\t  - the three-problem diagnosis (message-embedded identity, non-standard DSCI keys\n51\t    `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization`, missing `resourceKind`),\n52\t  - before/after code examples for converting message-embedded resource identity to\n53\t    structured key-value pairs, taken from the implemented conversion in the manager and\n54\t    cloudmanager binaries,\n55\t  - the DSCI key-name migration guide with before/after query examples for operators using\n56\t    Loki/CloudWatch queries that filtered on the old field names.\n57\t- Resolve, with PM / Observability team input, whether the convention should include\n58\t  fields beyond name/namespace/kind (e.g., reconciliation attempt count, error category)\n59\t  and document the decision — either included with rationale or explicitly deferred\n60\t  (weighing utility against log volume).\n61\t- Publish the convention as a specification for voluntary adoption by external operator\n62\t  teams — the Cluster Observability Operator team's Loki Operator and Tempo Operator — per\n63\t  platform policy (overlay 0008: RHOAI does not install, manage, or control external\n64\t  operator dependencies).\n65\t- File tracking issues in the COO projects for the convention's adoption, accepting that\n66\t  external adoption is best-effort.\n67\t\n68\t## Acceptance Criteria\n69\t\n70\t- The contribution guideline exists, specifying the required fields (`name`, `namespace`,\n71\t  `resourceKind`), the camelCase naming rationale, and the three-problem diagnosis.\n72\t- The guideline includes before/after code examples for converting message-embedded\n73\t  resource identity to structured key-value pairs, and a DSCI key migration guide with\n74\t  before/after query examples.\n75\t- The decision on additional convention fields (e.g., reconciliation attempt count, error\n76\t  category) is recorded with PM/Observability input: either included in the guideline with\n77\t  rationale or explicitly deferred with rationale.\n78\t- The convention is published for external operator adoption and tracking issues are filed\n79\t  in the COO (Loki Operator, Tempo Operator) projects.\n80\t- The guideline is technically reviewed against the implemented logging changes in the\n81\t  manager and cloudmanager binaries (examples match the shipped code, field names match the\n82\t  implementation).\n83\t\n84\t## HLR Traceability\n85\t\n86\t- HLR-8 [P1]: document the convention as a contribution guideline for new controller\n87\t  development and publish for external operator adoption.\n88\t- Strategy acceptance criterion: the structured log field convention is documented in a\n89\t  contribution guideline specifying required fields, camelCase naming rationale, and the\n90\t  three-problem diagnosis.\n91\t\n92\t## Risks / Notes\n93\t\n94\t- External operator adoption delay: the COO team may not prioritize adoption of the\n95\t  convention. Mitigation: publish the convention and file tracking issues; adoption is\n96\t  best-effort per platform policy (overlay 0008) and outside this strategy's control.\n97\t- This epic must run after the code conversion in both binaries so its before/after\n98\t  examples and migration guide reflect the implemented convention.\n99\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9d89b3ac798303c4","agent_id":"a677d7f0bb66f1eae","session_id":"97c222b8-155b-40d2-9c11-f4c45b15208c","uuid":"95b5fd95-9694-4f71-a01a-cecb8963b980","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:31:17.841Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9053212bb5a352eb","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
