{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-89a1258b8e5bd538","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E001\n3\ttitle: Standardize manager binary reconciliation error logs with structured resource\n4\t  context\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n6\tcomponent: OpenShift AI Productization\n7\tteam: ODH Operator team\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies: []\n11\tai_signals:\n12\t  change_specificity: 1\n13\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n14\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n15\t  existing_foundation: 1\n16\t  open_questions: 1\n17\t  external_dependency: 0\n18\t  human_process_gates: 0\n19\t  repo_access: 1\n20\t  architecture_claims: 1\n21\timplementation_type: null\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 6\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Standardize manager binary reconciliation error logs with structured resource context\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThis epic converts message-embedded resource identity to structured key-value pairs and\n35\tadds the `resourceKind` field across all reconciliation error logging in the rhods-operator\n36\tmanager binary. It delivers the three fixes diagnosed in the strategy for the manager\n37\tbinary: (1) reconciliation error logs that embed resource name or namespace in the message\n38\tstring are converted to structured `name`/`namespace` key-value pairs, (2) the\n39\tDSCInitialization controller is migrated from the non-standard key names `Request.Name` and\n40\t`DSCInitialization` to the standard camelCase convention (`name`, `namespace`,\n41\t`resourceKind`), and (3) `resourceKind` is added to all reconciliation error logs,\n42\tincluding controllers whose reconciler name does not imply the kind (service controllers,\n43\tmodule controller and its handlers, action files). A CI lint rule locks the convention in\n44\tfor future development, and a log-consumer regression validation protects existing\n45\tingestion pipelines and text-based alert rules.\n46\t\n47\t## Scope\n48\t\n49\t- Audit all `log.Error()` call sites in reconciliation error paths across the manager\n50\t  binary's five controller tiers:\n51\t  - the DataScienceCluster (DSC) controller,\n52\t  - 8 component controllers (DataSciencePipelines, Kueue, ModelRegistry, Ray,\n53\t    SparkOperator, Trainer, TrainingOperator, TrustyAI),\n54\t  - the module controller with its 8 module handlers (Dashboard, AIGateway, KServe, OGX,\n55\t    Workbenches, MLflowOperator, FeastOperator, MCPLifecycleOperator),\n56\t  - the DSCInitialization (DSCI) controller,\n57\t  - 5 service controllers (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup).\n58\t- Audit and convert the 15 action files across four tiers: 8 component action files\n59\t  (`components/<name>/<name>_controller_actions.go`), 3 service action files\n60\t  (`services/{auth,gateway,monitoring}/*_controller_actions.go`), 1 DSC action file\n61\t  (`datasciencecluster/datasciencecluster_controller_actions.go`), and 3 module action\n62\t  files (`modules/modules_controller_actions*.go`).\n63\t- For every call site embedding resource name or namespace in the message string, extract\n64\t  the identity fields and convert to structured key-value pairs\n65\t  (`\"name\", <obj>.Name, \"namespace\", <obj>.Namespace`), removing the redundant identity\n66\t  from the message text.\n67\t- Add `resourceKind` as a structured field to all reconciliation error logs: required for\n68\t  service controllers, the module controller and its handlers, and all action files (kind\n69\t  not implied by controller name), and for the DSC and 8 component controllers (bundled P1\n70\t  queryability enhancement over the same call sites).\n71\t- Migrate DSCI structured field names from `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` to\n72\t  `name`/`namespace` (per Staff Engineer input, at `dscinitialization_controller.go:154,169,182`).\n73\t- Handle cluster-scoped resources (e.g., DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization): emit\n74\t  `name` and `resourceKind`, with `namespace` omitted or set to empty string — no spurious\n75\t  namespace value.\n76\t- Add a CI lint/static-analysis rule that flags any `log.Error` call embedding\n77\t  name/namespace in message text or missing the required structured fields. The rule is\n78\t  path-scoped to the manager binary's directories so it does not gate the parallel\n79\t  cloudmanager conversion (see Risks/Notes).\n80\t- Add unit tests asserting field presence and correctness via test logger output.\n81\t- Log-consumer regression validation: before/after log output comparison for a sample\n82\t  reconciliation error; deploy a test build to a dev cluster with the production log\n83\t  consumer stack configured and verify ingestion; coordinate with SRE/Support to identify\n84\t  text-based alert rules that rely on the changed message-string patterns and track their\n85\t  updates.\n86\t\n87\t## Acceptance Criteria\n88\t\n89\t- Static analysis (grep/lint) over the manager binary finds zero `log.Error`\n90\t  reconciliation-error call sites that embed resource name or namespace in the message\n91\t  string; every such site emits `name` and `namespace` as structured key-value pairs.\n92\t- Unit tests assert DSCI error logs contain the standard field names (`name`,\n93\t  `namespace`, `resourceKind`), and a codebase grep confirms no references to the old\n94\t  field names `Request.Name` and `DSCInitialization` remain.\n95\t- The DSCI key-name migration lands as a single-release cutover — no release ships with\n96\t  both the old (`Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization`) and new (`name`/`namespace`) field\n97\t  names emitted for the same log calls — and the migration, with before/after\n98\t  Loki/CloudWatch query examples, is documented in that release's release notes.\n99\t- Unit tests parsing test logger output assert `resourceKind` is present with the correct\n100\t  value for error logs from all 5 service controllers (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring,\n101\t  CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup), the module controller and its 8 module handlers, and all\n102\t  15 action files across the 4 tiers.\n103\t- Unit tests assert DSC and 8 component controller reconciliation error logs include\n104\t  `resourceKind`.\n105\t- A unit test confirms cluster-scoped resources (e.g., DataScienceCluster,\n106\t  DSCInitialization) do not emit a spurious namespace value.\n107\t- The CI lint rule is merged, path-scoped to the manager binary, and demonstrably fails\n108\t  on a deliberately non-conforming `log.Error` call (test fixture) while passing on the\n109\t  converted manager binary.\n110\t- A before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error is documented,\n111\t  showing structured fields present and the message-text change, and confirming the log\n112\t  consumer (e.g., Loki) ingests both formats without configuration changes.\n113\t- Text-based alert rules relying on the changed message-string patterns are identified\n114\t  with SRE/Support, and each identified rule is recorded and tracked for update.\n115\t\n116\t## HLR Traceability\n117\t\n118\t- HLR-1 [P0]: reconciliation error logs embedding name/namespace in message strings\n119\t  converted to structured key-value pairs (manager binary portion).\n120\t- HLR-2 [P0]: DSCI controller migrated from `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` to\n121\t  camelCase `name`/`namespace`.\n122\t- HLR-3 [P0]: service controller error logs include `resourceKind`.\n123\t- HLR-4 [P0]: all 15 action file error logs include `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`\n124\t  across the 4 tiers (8 component + 3 service + 1 DSC + 3 module).\n125\t- HLR-6 [P0]: module controller error logs include `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`\n126\t  (8 module handlers).\n127\t- HLR-7 [P1] (bundled): DSC and component controller error logs include `resourceKind` —\n128\t  bundled because it edits the same `log.Error` call sites, shares the same audit pass and\n129\t  CI lint rule as the P0 conversion work; splitting would double-touch every call site.\n130\t\n131\t## Risks / Notes\n132\t\n133\t- Inconsistent adoption across the five controller tiers and 15 action files: mitigated by\n134\t  the grep/static-analysis audit with a coverage checklist and the CI lint rule gating new\n135\t  code.\n136\t- DSCI key-name migration replaces existing queryable field names: existing Loki/CloudWatch\n137\t  queries filtering on `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` will break. The transition is\n138\t  completed in a single release, and the migration is documented in release notes with\n139\t  before/after query examples (expanded in the convention documentation epic).\n140\t- Log consumer regression: addressed by the dev-cluster validation and SRE/Support alert\n141\t  rule identification above.\n142\t- The actual percentage of log calls embedding resource identity (SME estimate 75%) is\n143\t  confirmed by this epic's audit; the conversion covers all embedding sites regardless of\n144\t  the percentage.\n145\t- **CI lint rule scope and parallel-work coordination**: the lint rule created here is\n146\t  path-scoped to the manager binary's directories, so its \"passing\" AC is decoupled from\n147\t  the parallel cloudmanager conversion and the two epics remain independently schedulable\n148\t  (no dependency edge). Extending the rule's scope to the cloudmanager binary is handled\n149\t  within the cloudmanager conversion work after its call sites are converted; if the team\n150\t  instead opts to make the rule repo-wide, that change must be coordinated with the\n151\t  cloudmanager conversion timing so it does not gate unconverted code.\n152\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-817a130d001c7665","agent_id":"a7f75959f8ec75cb2","session_id":"97c222b8-155b-40d2-9c11-f4c45b15208c","uuid":"43c1d7da-94a1-4bff-8b08-1e7d0aa1afae","timestamp":"2026-10-25T19:39:43.933Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-89a1258b8e5bd538","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8010"}
