 E003 are Rule 11 (docs-last) edges, correctly\njustified in the DAG Justification table. E001 ∥ E002 parallelism is correct per Rule 15 (same repo,\ndisjoint binaries/controller sets); the shared CI lint rule is deliberately handled as a path-scoping\nAC plus a coordination note rather than a `dependencies` edge — the right shape, since a lint\nconfiguration is not a data/artifact dependency. No circular dependencies, no invalid edges, no\nkonflux/license/repo onboarding epics exist so Rules 7/8/10 cannot be violated. No branch files.\nCritical path length 2 matches the S-size heuristic (1-2). Cross-check of epic content found no\nuncaptured data/artifact dependency: E003's consumption of implemented before/after examples is\ncaptured by the two Rule 11 edges.\n\n### 3. Epic Boundaries (2/2)\n\nAll three epics carry the same validated component (`OpenShift AI Productization`, present in\n`.context/rhai-components.txt`) and team (ODH Operator team). The E001/E002 split along binary lines\nis a separate logical change, not a boundary violation — it makes the cloudmanager release-sequencing\ndecision (open question 3) a planning choice and keeps the epics independently schedulable. No scope\nduplication: E001 and E002 convert disjoint controller sets in disjoint binaries. No work-product\nmixing: code implementation (E001/E002) is separated from content authoring (E003). E001 exceeds the\n~2-week guideline, but the overage is acknowledged in Health Warnings with a concrete, measurable\nre-split trigger (controller-tier split if the audit finds ~2x the estimated call sites or conversion\noverruns the sprint) and the single-mechanical-pass rationale — a managed trade-off, not an\nunflagged overage, so the criterion is not docked.\n\n### 4. Type Correctness (2/2)\n\nE001 and E002 are Implementation epics producing concrete artifacts (converted log call sites, unit\ntests, CI lint rule, documented verification). E003 is correctly typed Implementation with\n`implementation