he\ncluster-scoped-resource AC and the static-analysis zero-remaining-sites measurement. Rule-mandated\nACs are present: the DSCI key-name replacement carries its Rule 23 compat mechanism as an explicit\nsingle-release-cutover AC with release-notes documentation (and the Health Warning explains why a\nfeature flag is inapplicable to log field names); the docs-authoring epic E003 has the technical\nreview AC (\"technically reviewed against the implemented logging changes... examples match the\nshipped code\"); no konflux chain exists so the build-pipeline AC does not apply. No soft-AC\nmisfiling found: the dev-cluster log-consumer verification and the SRE/Support alert-rule\nidentification are conditions on work the epics themselves perform and verify, not\nexternally-controlled preconditions. No epic body references sibling epics by draft ID — cross-epic\ncoordination is described by name (\"the parallel cloudmanager conversion\", \"the manager-binary\nwork\"), which survives Jira key assignment.\n\n### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n\nStrategy scope is fully accounted for: all three diagnosed problems, all five manager controller\ntiers plus the module controller's 8 handlers, all 15 action files (corrected counts per SME input:\n8 component + 3 service + 1 DSC + 3 module), all 3 cloudmanager controllers, the CI lint rule, the\nlog-consumer regression validation, the contribution guideline with its enumerated content, and the\nCOO publication/filing work. Strategy-level risks are carried forward to the right epics\n(inconsistent adoption → E001; log consumer regression → E001/E002; DSCI query breakage → E001 +\nHealth Warning; external adoption delay → E003), and all four open questions have explicit\ndispositions. Out-of-scope boundaries (non-reconciliation log paths, dashboards, external operator\nmanagement) are respected. One minor nit: E002's Risks/Notes state that extending the CI lint rule\nto cloudmanager paths \"is handled within the cloudmanager conversion work\"